the devastating effects of Manganese in humans (Levy
and Nassetta, 2003; Lawrence et al., 2009). Also
previous studies on the oil palm plantation have shown
that the soil has a pH of between 4 and 5 which is
acidic. The palm oil samples analysed did not reveal
elevated levels of Manganese element. Since the
concentrations of Manganese in all the oil samples
under investigation were below the WHO (2011)
permissible limits of Manganese also for vegetable
